xfce4-window-button-colors (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remove stored-colour management from the settings application (the
    "Stored window colours" list, per-row removal, and "Clean Up Orphaned
    Entries"). Clean Up Orphaned Entries caused real, reproduced data loss
    on the maintainer's own configuration, deleting colours for windows
    that were still open; the failure was not reliably reproducible from
    the same fixture and single click, so the defect could not be pinned
    down in the settings-app glue code. A button that sometimes destroys
    user data must not ship, so the section is withdrawn until the cause
    is found. The underlying reconciliation logic in src/core/ is
    unaffected and stays in place for the panel module and for when this
    feature returns. The settings binary no longer links libwnck.

 -- Jorge Alonso <desarrollos@enfoquestic.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 21:08:00 +0000

xfce4-window-button-colors (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the stored-colour list never appearing. The settings window probed
    the window manager's client list synchronously from its "map" handler,
    at which point the window is mapped but the WM has not yet processed
    it, so the completeness probe correctly judged the snapshot incomplete
    and nothing ever retried. The probe now runs one main-loop iteration
    later.

 -- Jorge Alonso <desarrollos@enfoquestic.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:00:00 +0000

xfce4-window-button-colors (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Adds the xfce4-window-button-colors-settings binary: a standalone
    GTK3 application, registered in the XFCE Settings Manager, that
    will host enabling/disabling the module and managing stored
    per-window colours without editing xfconf by hand. This release
    ships the application shell and packaging; the toggle and colour
    management UI land in a follow-up.
  * Adds libxfconf-0-dev to Build-Depends. The settings binary is the
    only target linking xfconf; src/core/ stays free of gtk_/xfconf_/
    wnck_ symbols, CI-enforced as before.

 -- Jorge Alonso <desarrollos@enfoquestic.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

xfce4-window-button-colors (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial package. Ships the GTK3 module and its CSS provider (slices
    1-3): colours are read from ~/.config/xfce4-window-button-colors/colors.css
    and painted onto matching launchers at panel start.
  * The context-menu item and the colour chooser are not implemented yet
    (slice 4), so colours must be written to colors.css by hand for now.
  * The module is installed but not enabled; see README for how to load it.

 -- Jorge Alonso <desarrollos@enfoquestic.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
